You need to pair ngrok with Port 80 because XSS Hunter Express expects to receive incoming web traffic over standard HTTP.
Run this command in a separate terminal tab:

ngrok http 80

## How the Pairing Works

[ Target Web App ] ---> (Hits Ngrok URL) ---> [ Ngrok Tunnel ] ---> [ Local Port 80 ] ---> [ Docker / XSS Hunter ]

## Steps to Link Them:

   1. Start Ngrok: Run ngrok http 80 and copy the public HTTPS forwarding URL (e.g., 1a2b-34-56.ngrok-free.app). Do not include https://.
   2. Update XSS Hunter Configuration: Open your configuration file:
   
   nano docker-compose.yml
   
   3. Insert the URL: Find the HOSTNAME line and change it to match your Ngrok URL:
   
   HOSTNAME: 1a2b-34-56.ngrok-free.app
   
   4. Launch the Server: Save the file and start your container instance with administrative privileges:
   
   sudo docker-compose up xsshunterexpress
   
   
